WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.100
Where does a motor neuron come from?

2
00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:10.820
In the neural tube, Sonic hedgehog sets up a gradient.

3
00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:17.920
Progenitors read their position in it, and one stripe, called pMN, makes motor

4
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:23.460
neurons. Yet a progenitor there does not contain a gene for motor neuron.

5
00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:27.140
It contains three or four transcription factors.

6
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.660
None is specific to motor neurons on its own.

7
00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:34.940
A motor neuron is what that particular set spells.

8
00:00:36.083 --> 00:00:40.943
Around its final division, a motor neuron turns on a new set.

9
00:00:41.743 --> 00:00:49.103
These are Isl1 or its relative Isl2, Lhx3, and Mnx1.

10
00:00:50.003 --> 00:00:54.843
They are the markers you stain for to find a newly differentiated motor neuron.

11
00:00:55.663 --> 00:01:01.543
But Lhx3 is also made in a neighbour of the motor neuron, the V2 interneuron.

12
00:01:01.543 --> 00:01:05.483
One protein sits in two different cell types.

13
00:01:06.284 --> 00:01:09.884
Now try an experiment in the chick neural tube.

14
00:01:10.564 --> 00:01:14.644
Put Lhx3 into cells that have no Isl1.

15
00:01:15.184 --> 00:01:17.424
You get V2 interneuron genes.

16
00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:19.764
The reason is a partner.

17
00:01:20.724 --> 00:01:25.184
Lhx3 binds a cofactor called NLI directly.

18
00:01:25.184 --> 00:01:28.724
That complex triggers V2 differentiation.

19
00:01:29.967 --> 00:01:34.507
Add Isl1 to the same cell, and the result changes.

20
00:01:35.587 --> 00:01:38.167
Isl1 competes for NLI.

21
00:01:38.807 --> 00:01:45.707
It displaces Lhx3 onto a high-affinity site in the C-terminal region of Isl1.

22
00:01:46.807 --> 00:01:50.807
The complex that forms then promotes motor neuron genes.

23
00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:56.600
So the cell is not reading a gene that says motor neuron.

24
00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:01.760
It is reading which assembly wins a competition for a shared partner.

25
00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:05.660
The competition is a contest for one binding site.

26
00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:09.000
Look at the same surface of Lhx3.

27
00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:11.960
It holds NLI in one complex.

28
00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:15.500
In the other, it holds a segment of Isl1.

29
00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:18.530
Two tests, two questions.

30
00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:26.170
Put Isl1 and Lhx3 together into one chick cell, and motor neuron genes come up.

31
00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:31.510
Delete Isl1 in the mouse, and motor neurons are not generated at all.

32
00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:35.070
Adding a factor shows what it can impose.

33
00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:39.030
Deleting it shows what cannot be built without it.

34
00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:46.690
Keep this rule. A motor neuron is spelled by a combination of factors, not by one master gene.
